<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n99839" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνεθ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accustom</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕτερον ἑτέρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					589a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τινὰ ποιεῖν τι</span>
			<i>accustom</i> him to do . . , <i><span class="en">
				D.
				13.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.24
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. [τὰ τέκνα] πρὸς τὰ ψύχη</span>
			<i>accustom</i> them to bear cold, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1336a13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>HA</u>
				567a6
			</span></i>; <i>make customary</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.107
			</span></i> K.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>become used</i> or <i>habituated</i>, and in
				aor. 1 and pf.
			<i>to have become so</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				146b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Plt.</u>
				285a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1340a16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.89
			</span></i>: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνειθίσθην ποιεῖν τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					2.38
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.14.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> to a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				917a15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.102
			</span></i> K.: impers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνειθισμένον ἦν</span>
			<i>it had become the custom</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr. in 
				Act.
			, <i>grow accustomed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς ἁπλαῖς . . διαίταις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					3p.64U.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				p.60
			</span></i> U.</div>
